        "explanation": "I left the TODO in place and made no edit to the file.\n\n**Issue 1 (line 323, `no-warning-comments`):** The comment `TODO Trigger their dispose callbacks.` is still accurate. `prunePaths` (lines 324–331) only runs the callbacks in `pruneMap`. It never touches `disposeMap`, so pruned modules' dispose callbacks are never called.\n\nThere are two ways to clear the warning, and neither fits the rules for this task:\n\n- **Delete or reword the comment.** This hides a real missing feature instead of fixing it.\n- **Do what the TODO says.** `prunePaths` would look up each path in `this.disposeMap`, call it with `this.dataMap.get(path)`, and wait for any returned promise before running the prune callbacks. That is how upstream Vite's HMR client does it. But it changes runtime behavior, and it would change the method from `void` to `async` returning `Promise<void>`, so every caller would need checking.\n\nWhoever owns this code should decide whether to implement dispose-on-prune. If they do, the comment can go in the same change."
      },
